 Framework for Evaluating and Aligning Emotional Intelligence in Spoken Language Models\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">C.9 </span>Prompt for Conflict Resolution and De-escalation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection\"><a href=\"#A3.SS10\" title=\"In Appendix C Detailed Prompt Templates for Data Construction ‣ EmoS: A Theory-Grounded Framework for Evaluating and Aligning Emotional Intelligence in Spoken Language Models\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_title\"><span class=\"ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref\">C.10 </span>Prompt for Value Alignment and Safety Response</span></a></li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol></nav>\n</nav>\n<div class=\"ltx_page_main\">\n<div id=\"infobox\" class=\"infobox\">\n  <a id=\"license-tr\" href=\"https://info.arxiv.org/help/license/index.html#licenses-available\">\n    License: CC BY 4.0\n  </a>\n  <div id=\"watermark-tr\">\narXiv:2608.09189v1 [cs.CL] 10 Aug 2026</div>\n</div><div class=\"ltx_page_content\">\n<article class=\"ltx_document ltx_authors_1line ltx_leqno\">\n<div id=\"p1\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n<span id=\"p1.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\setcctype</span>\n<p id=\"p1.2\" class=\"ltx_p\">by</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n<span id=\"p2.1\" class=\"ltx_ERROR undefined\">\\correspondingauthor</span>\n</div>\n<h1 class=\"ltx_title ltx_title_document\">EmoS: A Theory-Grounded Framework for Evaluating and Aligning Emotional Intelligence in Spoken Language Models</h1>\n<div class=\"ltx_authors\">\n<span class=\"ltx_creator ltx_role_author\">\n<span class=\"ltx_personname\">Junyu Wang\n</span><span class=\"ltx_author_notes\">\n<span class=\"ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation\"><span id=\"id1.1.id1\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_department\">Tianjin Key Laboratory of Cognitive Computing and Application</span><span id=\"id2.2.id2\" class=\"ltx_text ltx_affiliation_institution\">Tianjin University</span><span id=\"id3.3.id3\" cl